// Change: new rule
// Title: HackTool - SharpSCCM Execution
// Sigma ID: 97e45307-42b0-449d-bd9a-28bd6826c25c
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ashish Pulivarthy (ashish-cybersec)
// Date: 2026-07-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555, lateral-movement, T1187
// Description: Detects the execution of SharpSCCM, a post-exploitation tool that abuses Microsoft Endpoint
//   Configuration Manager (SCCM/ConfigMgr) for credential gathering and lateral movement without
//   requiring access to the SCCM administration console. The tool extracts DPAPI-protected policy
//   secrets-such as Network Access Account (NAA) credentials, task sequence variables, and
//   collection variables-from the local WMI repository or CIM store. It can also coerce NTLM
//   authentication from SCCM servers in sites where automatic site-wide client push installation is
//   enabled, potentially leading to site takeover. Because SCCM service accounts are frequently
//   highly privileged, successful use of this tool often results in the disclosure of domain-level
//   administrative credentials.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Mayyhem/SharpSCCM
//   - https://docs.specterops.io/sharpsccm-docs/resources/Command-Line-Usage
//   - https://blog.xpnsec.com/unobfuscating-network-access-accounts/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/57ac2bdde60ddfeb109364b9fbca9c44d3b011d5/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharpsccm.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SharpSCCM.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SharpSCCM.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "invoke client-push" or ProcessCommandLine contains "get site-push-settings") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "local site-info" or ProcessCommandLine contains "local user-sid")
